      <tr>
<th class="default">Title:</th>
<td class="default">Conductivity, Temperature and Depth (CTD) data from KAIMALINO, WECOMA and other platforms in the TOGA Area - Pacific from 1988-10-30 to 1991-12-09 (NCEI Accession 9500039)</td>
</tr>
      <tr>
<th class="default">Abstract:</th>
<td class="default_dark">The multiple sets of Conductivity, Temperature and Depth (CTD) data were collected in TOGA Area - Pacific (30 N to 30 S) as part of World Ocean Circulation Experiment (WOCE). Data was collected from ships A. AGASSIZ, MOANA WAVE, WECOMA, KAIMALINO by principal investigators from different Institutions. The data was collected over a period spanning from October 30, 1988 to December 9, 1991. Data was submitted by Steven M. Chiswell of Bundesamt für Seeschifffahrt und Hydrographie, Hamburg, Germany.</td>
</tr>
